🦈 Network Forensics & Traffic Analysis (Wireshark)
As a security analyst, I leverage Wireshark to perform deep packet interrogation, moving beyond simple observation to reconstruct attack stories from raw network data
. My proficiency covers the entire lifecycle of an investigation, from surgical filtering to payload extraction.
🔍 Core Investigative Techniques
The Forensic Mindset: I treat packet captures (PCAPs) as digital crime scenes, using TCP Stream Reconstruction to read full transcripts of attacker-victim conversations
.
Data Exfiltration Detection: I identify unauthorized data transfers by analyzing HTTP POST requests and sorting by packet size to find high-volume outbound flows
.
Beaconing Identification: I use I/O Graphs to visualize the "digital heartbeat" of compromised machines, spotting the rhythmic metronome patterns typical of Command & Control (C2) channels
.
Payload Extraction: I can surgically extract malicious files directly from the capture using Export Objects (HTTP/SMB) for isolated sandbox analysis
.
🛠️ Essential Display Filter Arsenal
I use precise display filters to cut through the noise of hundreds of thousands of packets and isolate critical evidence
.
Reconnaissance & Scanning
Filter
Operational Purpose
tcp.flags.syn == 1 && tcp.flags.ack == 0
SYN Scan Detection: Identifies rapid "knocks" on many ports with no intention of completing the handshake
.
icmp.type == 8
Ping Sweep: Detects attackers attempting to map active hosts on a subnet
.
tcp.flags.reset == 1
Connection Refusal: Spots where security controls or closed ports are blocking traffic
.
Command & Control (C2) & DNS Hunting
Filter
Operational Purpose
dns.qry.name.len > 50
DNS Tunneling: Finds suspiciously long domain names used to smuggle data out of the network
.
tls.handshake.type == 1
Client Hello Inspection: Identifies which external servers a host is attempting to connect to via SNI, even in encrypted traffic
.
tcp.port == 4444
Uncommon C2 Ports: Specifically monitors ports frequently used by malicious frameworks
.
Web & Data Integrity
Filter
Operational Purpose
http.request.method == "POST"
Data Submission: Monitors for exfiltration or credential harvesting via web forms
.
http contains "password"
Cleartext Leakage: Performs a raw byte search for unencrypted sensitive credentials
.
ip.addr == [Target IP]
Host Isolation: Focuses the entire capture on traffic involving one specific machine
.
